{"kind":"assert","text":"Amendment to ruling b02334db after the checker's answer b0b989ec. The\nchecker has no objection. I accept its four points. The offline\ncaller-record plumbing goes, and the slice may start.\n\n1. A second fixed place. `genesis.message.body.directory` names a\n   Directory by its place, as the platform writes it in every `create`\n   of a lane. Item 3 and the section 8 paragraph gain it: \"A grant and\n   a creation context name a Membership by their place, and the\n   `directory` of a lane's creation names a Directory.\"\n2. A kind in a state record. A Hold prices a standing `receiver-pin`\n   by the kind of the record's `task` (`hold.ts:1053`). `licensed`\n   writes the kind into the record beside `task`. It takes the kind\n   from the `sourceKind` of the entry that it judges, and from nowhere\n   else. The price keeps its dependence on the kind. The rule is\n   general: a state record that a later judgment prices or branches on\n   by the kind of a sequence holds that kind, copied from the entry\n   that checked it. Name any other such record that the inventory\n   finds.\n3. Native identity. `EvidenceView.lane` and `rootCreation` in\n   packages/replay/src/identity.ts read the creator's birth through\n   `birth()`. In `lane(at)`, the `seed.kind` of that birth must be\n   `lane`, and a difference refuses the identity proof. Add the\n   witness: a child that records `sourceKind` `lane` over a creator of\n   another kind reaches no Native identity result. This is in the\n   slice.\n4. Archive names. `#anchoredPrivateName` checks that the catalog kind\n   of the manifest row's pin equals the kind that the receiving entry\n   records, in `sourceKind` or in `FactUse.kind`. A row cannot pair a\n   Membership pin with a sender that the entry records as a Register.\n\nEverything else in b02334db stands.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}